sentences.l:
He spoke, and having brandished it he sent forth his long-shadowed spear,
and hit him, and did not miss, aiming at the head,
on the top of the helmet;

And Hector quickly ran back an immeasurable way, and mingled with the throng,
and stood on his knees, having crashed down, and propped himself with a stout hand
on the earth;

He then, for his part, the breastplate of mighty Agastrophus
was taking from his chest, and the all-glancing shield from his shoulders,
and the weighty helmet;

and he drew back the arm of the bow
and hit him, and then the shaft did not escape him from his hand in vain,
the flat of the right foot;

And Chersidamas then, as he leapt down from his horses,
with a spear in the lower belly, beneath his bossed shield,
he stabbed;
